pport vectors will change  the position of the hyperplane these are  the main points that help us build our  svm in linear svm the resulting  separating plane is the same space as  your input features therefore its  coefficients can be viewed as weights of  the inputs dimensions and we can use  these weights to select top features  that are responsible for model accuracy  now that we've completed this review let  us turn to another important topic for  machine learning parametric  classification and regression so let's  now speak about generalized linear  models  first  let's talk about linear regression  variables are terms we use to define our  data in an experiment  any externally controlled variable  related to data collection is called an  independent variable it is manipulated  by what we intend to study  the data we collect are the dependent  variables  these variables represent the  measurements we take of the conditions  in the experiment  oftentimes we would like to establish a  relationship between changes in  independent variable to establish the  relationship of measured dependent  variables with the cause we control  sometimes this cause can be indirect and  therefore not a causal effect even  though it appears to be so  nevertheless establishing a non-random  relationship between the two  is important  let's say we collect the data on eye  color  sex  age height and weight of people  we hypothesize that some variables here  are related and some are not we also  think there are exceptions to the rule  the age and height or weight are related  but maybe not always relationships  observed in data can show which  variables are related or unrelated and  if related then by how much for example  weight and height seem to be logically  related  are they in this data set if we plot a  trend line we will find that the trend  line goes up the bigger the height  weight is also increasing  but the dots are not too close to the  line some dots seem to be far away from  the line  is there a way to quantify this  relationship we found  to study the relationship we can use a  coefficient of correlation or r squared  this measure shows how well the data in  our data set is explained by the  correlation line drawn through this data  in this case we get an r squared  coefficient of 41  40 is okay but not perfect our  conclusion is that height and weight are  correlated but not perfectly  such relationships can be of several  types positive negative and non-linear  linear regression is a way to further  model such a relationship to determine a  mathematical function explaining the  relationship between a dependent and  independent variable in the data set  if there is a relationship such a  function is predictive and will inform  us how the independent variable will  change if we change the dependent  variable  the goal of regression analysis is to  find the right coefficients of this  formula that minimize predictive errors  based on the data that we have the  regression formula has both the  dependent and independent variables in a  mathematical equation plus a constant  intercept and a coefficient  the dependent variable is related  to the independent variable with  additional considerations a constant  intercept or where the line starts from  the slope of the regression line also  known as the coefficient  to get these variables from data we use  the least squares approach it helps  measure the distance from each dot to a  line finding the line that best fits the  data  simple linear regression is an approach  to model the relationship between a  dependent variable and one independent  variable the linear regression model  assumes a linear relationship between  the input and output variables  if this relationship is present we can  estimate the coefficients required by  the model to make predictions on new  data  same principles can be applied in anova  where variables are factors and factor  regression analysis factor regressio